r electronic processing, but in modern times, that distinction has been lost because almost all recorded music today, and the majority of live music performances, depend on extensive use of electronics.", "url": null, "artists": [{"artist": "BTS", "streams": 173294, "best_position": 16}, {"artist": "Arctic Monkeys", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Beyonc\u00e9", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Billie Eilish", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Britney Spears", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Charli xcx", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Daddy Yankee", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Daft Punk", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Dua Lipa", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Gorillaz", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Jimin", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Jung Kook", "streams": null, "best_position": null}]}, "electropop": {"genre": "electropop", "country_code": "co", "country_name": "Colombia", "summary": "Electropop is a type of electronic pop music which features crackly synthesizers prominently in the mix.   Electropop has become an increasingly common term for this music post-2000 whereas in earlier years, synthpop was probably the more common term for pop music using synthesizers.\n\nWhen Kraftwerk first appeared in the mid-1970's, their music was described as electronic body music (ebm) in Germany, Krautrock in England, and technopop in Japan.", "url": null, "artists": [{"artist": "AD\u00c9LA", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Beyonc\u00e9", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Billie Eilish", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Britney Spears", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Charli xcx", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Dua Lipa", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Gorillaz", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "KATSEYE", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Katy Perry", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Lady Gaga", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Madonna", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Miley Cyrus", "streams": null, "best_position": null}]}, "hip-hop": {"genre": "hip-hop", "country_code": "co", "country_name": "Colombia", "summary": "Hip-Hop, also spelled Hip Hop or HipHop is a rhythm focused popular music style, originating from New York in The 70s. The term rap is sometimes used synonymously with Hip-Hop music. Hip-hop arose when DJs began isolating the percussion break from funk or disco songs for audiences to dance to.\nIt is now seen as a worldwide and popular genre ranging from American Mainstream (e.g. Eminem, Lil Wayne) to British Underground (e.g. Wiley, EMC Junkie ect).", "url": null, "artists": [{"artist": "Omar Courtz", "streams": 177674, "best_position": 22}, {"artist": "Bad Bunny", "streams": 149571, "best_position": 41}, {"artist": "Anuel AA", "streams": 110745, "best_position": 14}, {"artist": "Plan B", "streams": 81827, "best_position": 39}, {"artist": "J Balvin", "streams": 76581, "best_position": 46}, {"artist": "Agust D", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Alvaro Diaz", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Beyonc\u00e9", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Bizarrap", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Daddy Yankee", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Daft Punk", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Doja Cat", "streams": null, "best_position": null}]}, "k-pop": {"genre": "k-pop", "country_code": "co", "country_name": "Colombia", "summary": "K-pop means Korean pop, which is\u00a0a musical genre, sometimes described more as an umbrella term, consisting of different music styles, including hip-hop, rap, jazz, r&b, dance, rock music and ballads. The name for the genre is first recorded in English around 1990\u201395. Strongly influenced by Western popular music, K-pop took off in 1992 with Seo Taiji and Boys, who incorporated rap, rock, and dance elements into Korean popular music.\nModern\u00a0K-pop \"idol\" culture\u00a0began later in the 1990s, as K-pop idol music grew into a\u00a0subculture.", "url": null, "artists": [{"artist": "BTS", "streams": 173294, "best_position": 16}, {"artist": "Agust D", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "ILLIT", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Jimin", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Jung Kook", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "KATSEYE", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "LE SSERAFIM", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "NewJeans", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "TWICE", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "j-hope", "streams": null, "best_position": null}]}, "latin": {"genre": "latin", "country_code": "co", "country_name": "Colombia", "summary": "Latin American music or Latin music encompasses rhythms and styles originated or related to Latin America and its influence in the United States and several European countries such as Spain or Portugal. Some critics have defined Latin music as an incorporation of four elements: music style, geography, cultural background of the artist and language. The first of those encapsulates all music styles generated from Latin countries, such as salsa, merengue.", "url": null, "artists": [{"artist": "KAROL G", "streams": 672987, "best_position": 1}, {"artist": "Ryan Castro", "streams": 296843, "best_position": 35}, {"artist": "Arc\u00e1ngel", "streams": 263747, "best_position": 54}, {"artist": "Feid", "streams": 244294, "best_position": 5}, {"artist": "Omar Courtz", "streams": 177674, "best_position": 22}, {"artist": "Bad Bunny", "streams": 149571, "best_position": 41}, {"artist": "Maluma", "streams": 139706, "best_position": 50}, {"artist": "Anuel AA", "streams": 110745, "best_position": 14}, {"artist": "J Balvin", "streams": 76581, "best_position": 46}, {"artist": "Alvaro Diaz", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Bizarrap", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Daddy Yankee", "streams": null, "best_position": null}]}, "nu metal": {"genre": "nu metal", "country_code": "co", "country_name": "Colombia", "summary": "Nu metal is a subgenre of alternative metal that blends elements of heavy metal with influences from other genres such as hip hop, funk, industrial, and grunge. It typically emphasises rhythm and syncopation, with guitar work often involving down-tuned seven-string guitars to create a heavier sound. Guitar solos and technical displays are generally less common in nu metal. Vocal styles vary and may include singing, rapping, screaming, and occasionally growling.", "url": null, "artists": [{"artist": "Deftones", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Linkin Park", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "System of a Down", "streams": null, "best_position": null}]}, "pop": {"genre": "pop", "country_code": "co", "country_name": "Colombia", "summary": "Pop music is a broad-term for many different types of music: The term is flexible, and the music labeled \"pop\" changes frequently. It usually refers to popular, appealing and mostly mainstream music with emphasis on catchy melodies and an accessible style, with songs that tend to have a short to medium length. Some subgenres may include synthpop, electropop, bubblegum, sophisti-pop, hyperpop and many others.", "url": null, "artists": [{"artist": "KAROL G", "streams": 672987, "best_position": 1}, {"artist": "Ryan Castro", "streams": 296843, "best_position": 35}, {"artist": "BTS", "streams": 173294, "best_position": 16}, {"artist": "Maluma", "streams": 139706, "best_position": 50}, {"artist": "J Balvin", "streams": 76581, "best_position": 46}, {"artist": "AD\u00c9LA", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Alvaro Diaz", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Arctic Monkeys", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Ariana Grande", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Beyonc\u00e9", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Billie Eilish", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Bizarrap", "streams": null, "best_position": null}]}, "post-punk": {"genre": "post-punk", "country_code": "co", "country_name": "Colombia", "summary": "Post-punk (originally called new musick) is a broad genre of music that emerged in late 1977 in the wake of punk rock. Post-punk musicians departed from punk's fundamental elements and raw simplicity, instead adopting a broader, more experimental approach that encompassed a variety of avant-garde sensibilities and non-rock influences. Inspired by punk's energy and do it yourself ethic but determined to break from rock cliches, artists experimented with styles like funk.", "url": null, "artists": [{"artist": "Arctic Monkeys", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Mac DeMarco", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Soda Stereo", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "The Cure", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "The Smiths", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "The Strokes", "streams": null, "best_position": null}]}, "r&b": {"genre": "r&b", "country_code": "co", "country_name": "Colombia", "summary": "R&B is a musical genre that began to develop as a distinct style in the early 1950s. Originally known as rhythm and blues, it was primarily created by African American musicians and drew influence from both blues and early rock 'n' roll, with significant interaction between these genres. Over time, musicians from different backgrounds adopted the style and introduced new elements. In the 1